issue_context.body:
It would be great to have vite running in a github codespace container.
Right now it works, but without Websockets because of the [port forwarding](https://docs.github.com/en/github/developing-online-with-codespaces/developing-in-a-codespace#forwarding-ports).

Codespace will forward eg. port 3000 to an xxxx.apps.codespaces.githubusercontent.com (port 80).
Vite tries to connect to the port which is a [global constant](https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/36422c2d5e0e0e59ef969d0b5287d98bfe7cc3ee/src/client/client.ts#L33) and is different then the proxied port.

```js
console.log('[vite] connecting...');
const socketProtocol = location.protocol === 'https:' ? 'wss' : 'ws';
const socketUrl = `${socketProtocol}://${location.hostname}:${3000}`;
const socket = new WebSocket(socketUrl, 'vite-hmr');
```

When serverd via the codespace server proxy, port 80 is mapped to 3000 internally. So we would need to adjust the __port__ accordingly when using codespace.
